    explanation: "Goals for the provision of post cardiac arrest care include: • Avoidance of hypotension (provision of isotonic fluids, vaso- pressors, and inotropic agents to maintain blood pressure .5th percentile for age). • Avoidance of fever with continuous core body temperature monitoring and targeted temperature management to maintain normothermia. Therapeutic hypothermia can be considered following out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA). • Avoidance of significant hypocapnia/hypercapnia or hypoxemia/ hyperoxia. • Monitoring for seizures.",
