    explanation: "As epithelium proliferates rapidly, the temporary occlusion of the larynx ends by the 10th week when recanalization occurs. Atresia is the least common result of failure to recanalize. Laryngeal webs and/ or stenosis may be common results of failure to recanalize. Branchial arches involved in embryogenesis of the larynx are as follows: carti- lages and muscles are derived from the fourth and sixth branchial arches, whereas the third and fourth branchial arches form the epiglottis by mesenchyme proliferation. Derivation of epithelium is from endoderm of the laryngotracheal tube, not mesoderm.",
