    correctAnswer: "B",
    correctAnswerText: "Methylation",
    explanation: "– 2. A lobule/acinus with poor compliance (low compliance) and low airways resistance will have the shortest filling time (RC time constant). This is because airways resistance is low allowing for faster transit time through the airway, and lung compliance is low causing rapid filling of the airspace. Both airways resistance and lung compliance being low lead to a short time constant. In ARDS, which is a heterogeneous lung disease, there are varying resistances and compliances (RC time constants) throughout the lung. This makes treating ARDS with mechanical ventilation a challenge.",
