    correctAnswer: "B",
    correctAnswerText: "Start nitric oxide at 20 ppm.",
    explanation: "The echocardiogram indicates elevated pulmonary vascular resistance based on the tricuspid valve jet and right ventricular dysfunction. Inhaled nitric oxide is a specific pulmonary vasodilator that may be useful in augmenting cardiac output.",
