    title: "Identify and provide the value of the pressure waveform shown in the Figure, which was taken from a...",
    scenario: "Identify and provide the value of the pressure waveform shown in the Figure, which was taken from a patient on positive-pressure mechanical ventilation.",
    choices: {"A": "Pulmonary artery pressure, 47/27 mm Hg", "B": "Pulmonary artery pressure, 30/20 mm Hg", "C": "Pulmonary artery occlusion pressure, 34 mm Hg", "D": "Pulmonary artery occlusion pressure, 19 mm Hg"},
    correctAnswer: "D",
    correctAnswerText: "Pulmonary artery occlusion pressure, 19 mm Hg",
    explanation: "Rationale This is a pulmonary artery occlusion pressure (PAOP) with a dominant and elevated v wave that could be confused with a pulmonary artery (PA) waveform. However, in timing with the ECG, it is apparent that the peak of the v wave occurs after the T wave of the ECG, whereas the peak systolic pressure of the PA waveform would occur in timing with the T wave. Both a and c waves are discernible in this PAOP, facilitating measurement of the pre-c wave at end-expiration, just before the pressure starts to rise, with a value of 19 mm Hg, which is elevated.",
