    scenario: "An otherwise healthy adolescent with septic shock has a central mixed venous oxygen saturation (ScvO2) of 50% after 40 mL/kg of normal saline boluses and intubation. In considering packed erythrocyte transfusion in this patient, what are the current evidence-based thresholds for transfusion during initial goal-directed sepsis resuscitation and the recommended subsequent treatment for critically ill children? Initial Goal-Directed Sepsis Resuscitation (g/dL/%) Recommended ICU Treatment for Critically Ill Children (g/dL/%) A Hb~7/Hct~20 Hb~7/Hct~20 B Hb~10/Hct~30 Hb~10/Hct~30 C Hb~7/Hct~20 Hb~10/Hct~30 D Hb~10/Hct~30 Hb~7/Hct~20 E Hb~10/Hct~30 Prescribe erythropoietin at Hb~10/Hct~30",
